Fixed importing a principal document that held a value of the wrong type, an id the site cannot use, or a role it does not define. The dry run reported such a document fine, and the import then failed partway through. Now a wrong type refuses the document before anything is written, naming the record and the key. A user or group whose id its container refuses is skipped, and a role the site does not define is left out and reported. A dry run now also reports a group whose `container_group` does not exist, and an identity claimed by two users in the same document, as the import does. @ericof
